$
  omega^((2)) = omega_(12) d x^1 and d x^2 + omega_(34) d x^3 and d x^4; \
  Omega^((4)) = 1/(2!) omega and omega
  = 1/(2!) (2 omega_(12) omega_(34) d x^1 and d x^2 and d x^3 and d x^4) = \
  = (omega_(12) omega_(34)) d x^1 and dots and d x^4; \
  f^2 lr((x)) = det(omega_(i j)) = (omega_(12) omega_(34))^2; quad
  f lr((x)) = omega_(12) omega_(34) = plus.minus sqrt(det(omega_(i j))).
$
